I'll fix the kanban store to properly listen to activeProject changes through the projects store mutations instead of using the undefined `$storex.watch`.

## Analysis

The issue is that `$storex.watch` doesn't exist. Instead, we should:
1. Trigger kanban reset/reload when `activeProjectChanged` action is called in projects store
2. Add a hook in the kanban store's `init()` action to subscribe to project changes
3. Use the projects store's mutations to detect changes

## Changes Summary

| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `src/store/kanban.js` | Removed `$storex.watch` approach, added `subscribeToProjectChanges()` helper, modified `init()` to set up proper listeners |
| `src/store/project.js` | Added call to notify kanban store when active project changes |

---

